[interviewer · RECOMMENDATION · 13:39] What's your recommendation to the CEO?

[candidate · 15:09] My recommendation: raise menu prices in stages, starting with roughly 10-12% now, and pair it with procurement renegotiation.

Why. The entire margin decline is explained by input inflation — beans up 40%, other inputs up 37.5%, which together account for all 16 points of the COGS increase. Menu prices haven't moved in two years, so Brew & Bean absorbed 100% of it. This is a pass-through failure, not an operational one. Overhead moved 2 points and labor is flat, so there's little to cut.

Risks. Volume loss if competitors held prices, and brand damage from a visible jump. Mitigate by testing in 15-20 stores first and staging increases rather than one large move.

Next steps. One, get competitor pricing to size the headroom. Two, pilot the increase and measure volume elasticity. Three, in parallel, renegotiate bean and dairy contracts at 200-store scale and look at hedging. Four, check waste rates — if spoilage is inflating COGS, that's margin with no customer impact.
